\b Read this before you install it.\b0\par
\par
This software supervises energy, water and alarm systems. It is \b not\b0  a protection system. Breakers, relief valves, float switches, high-limit thermostats and emergency stops retain authority over the equipment they protect, and nothing here gets a vote on that. The platform requests; local controllers decide.\par
\par
Physical control is disabled by default and should stay disabled until the subsystem you intend to control has passed commissioning. See docs/commissioning.md.\par
\par
\b Your data stays where it is.\b0\par
\par
Operator data \endash  the database, the alarm and command history, the logs, local backups and your configuration \endash  lives in %ProgramData%\\Project CHAOS and is \b not\b0  removed when you uninstall this product. Upgrading does not overwrite your configuration files either. If you want that data gone, delete it deliberately; the installer will not do it for you.\par
\par
\b The web interface is reachable on your LAN.\b0\par
\par
Installing adds one inbound Windows Firewall rule: TCP 8080, private networks only, so phones, tablets and wall displays on the homestead network can reach the interface. It is never opened on a public network profile. The rule is removed when you uninstall.\par
